WEBVTT

00:12:27.196 --> 00:12:30.636
which will basically prove the case

00:12:30.676 --> 00:12:37.436
that this is the number one thing
that parents want.

00:12:37.476 --> 00:12:39.996
And this will be a driver
of who they work for

00:12:39.996 --> 00:12:41.596
and who they don't work for.

00:12:41.636 --> 00:12:45.476
So it makes business sense if you care
about attrition, if you care about, again,

00:12:45.476 --> 00:12:48.236
the four million people
that are leaving every month.

00:12:48.276 --> 00:12:51.916
The way to retain them,
the way to win that talent war

00:12:51.916 --> 00:12:53.716
is to provide childcare.

00:12:53.716 --> 00:12:57.556
WPR: There’s a question from TED Member
Charlotte about a women’s general strike.

00:12:57.556 --> 00:12:58.956
What do you think about that?

00:12:58.996 --> 00:13:01.596
RS: Oh, I love it, the Iceland
strike, oh my God, yes.